 2 \\) cups (for half a cup plants) + \\( 8 \\) cups (for 1 cup plants) + \\( 2 \\) cups (for quarter cup plants) = \\( 2 + 8 + 2 = 12 \\) cups\n\nAnswer: 12", "output_sha256": "2add705039c1c09213758f575869b3712ebad95a263ca6fc72c9449975350660", "gold": "12", "ts": 1790125931.7905705}
{"id": "gsm8k/test/827", "group": "gsm8k/test/827", "source": "gsm8k", "kind": "number", "tier": "local", "model": "qwen2.5:3b-instruct", "correct": false, "y_error": 1, "features": {"req_tokens_log": 4.912654885736052, "req_messages": 1.0, "req_structured": 0.0, "req_tool": 0.0, "req_code": 0.0, "req_length": 0.2, "req_has_system": 0.0, "intent": "math", "data_class": "Public", "ret_top_sim": null, "ret_margin": null, "ret_coverage": null, "ret_verifier": null, "ret_sources": null, "ret_age_days_log": null, "ret_mismatch": null, "gen_mean_logprob": -0.13643161979734775, "gen_min_logprob": -1.784645438194275, "gen_p10_logprob": -0.5403916239738464, "gen_mean_entropy": 0.27305389782809686, "gen_mean_margin": 7.093346879321878, "gen_frac_low_conf": 0.06479481641468683, "gen_stop_length": 0.0, "gen_out_tokens_log": 6.142037405587356, "gen_schema_valid": null, "gen_refusal": 0.0, "gen_hedge_rate": 0.0, "gen_truncated_ctx": 0.0, "gen_answer_marker": 1.0, "gen_self_contradiction": 0.0, "sys_queue_depth": 0.0, "sys_ttft_log": 4.348464434875741, "sys_mem_pressure": 0.12115404483513026}, "prompt_tokens": 135, "completion_tokens": 464, "ttft_ms": 76.35958099854179, "total_ms": 8384.426948003238, "finish_reason": "stop", "output": "To determine how much money Milly will lose, we need to calculate the shipping cost and the refund amount, then find the difference between these two amounts.\n\n### Step 1: Calculate the Shipping Cost\nThe cost structure for shipping the book includes two components: the per-pound charge and the per-mile charge.\n\n- **Per-pound charge**: $0.35 per pound\n- **Per-mile charge**: $0.08 per mile\n- **Weight of the book**: 4 pounds\n- **Distance to the distribution center**: 20 miles\n\nFirst, calculate the per-pound charge:\n\\[ \\text{Per-pound charge} = 4 \\text{ pounds} \\times 0.35 \\text{ dollars/pound} = 1.40 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nNext, calculate the per-mile charge:\n\\[ \\text{Per-mile charge} = 20 \\text{ miles} \\times 0.08 \\text{ dollars/mile} = 1.60 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nNow, add these two charges to get the total shipping cost:\n\\[ \\text{Total shipping cost} = 1.40 \\text{ dollars} + 1.60 \\text{ dollars} = 3.00 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\n### Step 2: Calculate the Refund Amount\nAmazon will refund 75% of the book's purchase price.\n\n- **Purchase price of the book**: $32\n- **Refund percentage**: 75%\n\nCalculate the refund amount:\n\\[ \\text{Refund amount} = 32 \\text{ dollars} \\times 0.75 = 24 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\n### Step 3: Calculate the Net Loss\nThe net loss is the total shipping cost minus the refund amount:\n\\[ \\text{Net loss} = 3.00 \\text{ dollars} - 24 \\text{ dollars} = -21.00 \\text{ dollars} \\]\n\nSince the net loss is negative, Milly will actually gain money, not lose it. Therefore, Milly will gain $21.00.\n\nAnswer: -21.00", "output_sha256": "b1efea0b39564ab371a977210daec59b504105a5029af61c7d577ddbf2f8a3df", "gold": "11", "ts": 1790125931.7975173}
