outside party acquired the house at the foreclosure sale. The mortgage to the bank has priority, so the outside party received the house free of the mortgage to the bank. However, the mortgage to the credit union is still valid and encumbers the house. The outside party is not entitled to the $5,000 because the mortgage to the credit union is not extinguished by the foreclosure sale.\n\nGiven the above points, the $5,000 should go to the credit union because the mortgage to the bank has priority and the mortgage to the credit union is subordinate.\n\nAnswer: <D>", "output_sha256": "5ea9190475152026b86cf8e661911b22b3a56cfa52ba8b261f6254e33c98f232", "gold": "A", "ts": 1790125945.683483}
