tive of the statute of limitations.\n- This is incorrect because changes in accounting methods typically require a change in the tax year, not retroactively.\n\nD. The adjustment is improper because the statute of limitations has expired for several years of the adjustment.\n- This is correct because the statute of limitations for tax adjustments generally does not expire, and it would have expired by year 6.\n\nAnswer: D", "output_sha256": "e158d99ad6c92022244e84a60f42d44b7a6076581ad0a1dc0ac15d22ea83be82", "gold": "D", "ts": 1790125959.7705016}
