 used to establish a direct connection so that the data can be transmitted.\n- This option is incorrect because packets contain both data and metadata. Metadata is necessary for routing and delivery, but data is also crucial for the packet to be meaningful.\n\nD. Each packet contains multiple data files bundled together, along with metadata describing how to categorize each data file.\n- This option is not accurate. Data files are not typically bundled together in packets. Each packet contains a single data file or part of a file.\n\nAnswer: A", "output_sha256": "f7b8c07679ab87ea22357439c45d4afd12a0234afc20cba02e621e601b36e1d6", "gold": "A", "ts": 1790125965.2043135}
