ve measure but a regulatory one.\n\nThe equal protection clause of the Fourteenth Amendment is concerned with the treatment of individuals by the government, not with the content of publications or the freedom of the press.\n\nThe privileges or immunities clause of the Fourteenth Amendment is concerned with the rights of individuals to be protected from state interference with their privileges and immunities, which does not directly apply to the tax on newspapers.\n\nAnswer: D", "output_sha256": "741376f2ba0ee948cf68f7aa264c0ea25b79323c04d8b55fc7f00b488d1df3cb", "gold": "D", "ts": 1790125990.3582766}
