housand envelopes, which is not included in the initial offer.\n\nNow, let's evaluate the options:\n\nA. A contract at $1,000 because the offer terms CIF means cost, insurance and freight including all loading charges.\n   - This is incorrect because the CIF term does not include the loading charges, and the order confirmation specifies a loading charge.\n\nB. A contract at $1,500 because the loading charges are to be included.\n   - This is incorrect because the initial offer was for $1,000, and the order confirmation specifies a loading charge, not an additional amount.\n\nC. No contract because the order confirmation was a counteroffer which was not accepted.\n   - This is incorrect because the order confirmation accepted the initial offer and specified additional terms, which were accepted.\n\nD. No contract because the purchase order was the offer and, under the mirror image rule, can not be deviated from.\n   - This is incorrect because the purchase order accepted the terms of the initial offer, and the order confirmation accepted the terms of the purchase order, including the additional loading charges.\n\nConsidering the above analysis, the most likely correct answer is:\n\nAnswer: C", "output_sha256": "4177e3c0fa5c7626266408bc72aa32b3c991ea8b0adc79d66bd4b9a16a4c7753", "gold": "C", "ts": 1790126013.4114888}
