: The son conveyed the tract of land to his friend in 2005, but this conveyance was not recorded until after the son's death in 2009. Since the bank's mortgage was recorded in 2008, it would be effective against the friend, who did not record the conveyance before the mortgage was recorded.\n\nGiven these points, the most probable legal effect is that the subsequent mortgagee (the bank) would prevail as against the prior conveyee (the friend), who failed to record before the mortgage was effectuated.\n\nAnswer: D", "output_sha256": "f52ed13d882ae17cf0b7fa260d1d1b9b9fadec6f683a52b5006627b593f5484f", "gold": "D", "ts": 1790126022.2862139}
