ony murder regardless of whether the death was caused by the felony or another act. This would not apply here since the defendants did not cause the fracture.\n- **Proximate cause theory**: This theory holds that the defendant is only liable for the consequences of their own actions. Since the fracture was caused by the victim, the defendants would not be liable under this theory.\n- **Agency theory**: This theory holds that if a defendant is in the \"zone of danger\" during the commission of a felony, they can be held liable for any deaths that occur. In this case, the defendants were in the zone of danger and could be held liable for the death caused by the fracture.\n\nGiven the scenario, the best defense would be the **agency theory**.\n\nAnswer: D", "output_sha256": "a5401c218d89217ef6710c75420a8a7fe5135fc53b4ea660469817977c1be56e", "gold": "B", "ts": 1790126032.823955}
