ential subdivision similar to the eastern tract, subject to the residential restrictions.\n\n3. **Land Development Company's Instrument**: The land-development company's instrument of March 2001 released the land to the country club, but this does not affect the existing restrictions. The country club still needs to comply with the residential restrictions of the eastern tract.\n\n4. **Homeowners' Standing**: The homeowners in the western tract are not directly affected by the country club's proposed construction. The restrictions apply to the eastern tract, not the western tract. Therefore, the homeowners in the western tract do not have standing to challenge the country club's proposed construction plan.\n\nGiven these points, the most likely outcome is that the homeowners in the western tract will not succeed in their action to enjoin construction.\n\nAnswer: C", "output_sha256": "2aa266ca42fa8ba7feedfc0442c5dadfe2eda22e15b6b435c10bc2cfa8808e30", "gold": "C", "ts": 1790126050.8719692}
