s of Array A, and for each element, it accesses the corresponding element in Array B. The operation `A[i] = A[i] + B[2*i]` involves reading from both arrays and writing to Array A.\n\n4. **Memory Access and Write Through Policy**: Since the cache has a write-through policy, any write to the cache will be written to the main memory. The loop will write to the cache for each element of Array A, and since the write-through policy is in effect, these writes will be reflected in the main memory.\n\n5. **Counting Writes**: Each write to the cache corresponds to a write to the main memory. Since the loop iterates 256 times (one for each element in Array A), there will be 256 writes to the main memory.\n\nTherefore, the number of bytes written to memory is 256 bytes.\n\nAnswer: C", "output_sha256": "5f514141e4b5e8823427a27157b7684f620c505e51a1b18f7679c666aa6e0c87", "gold": "C", "ts": 1790128727.5611372}
