ta cache without changing the clock cycle time: The size of the cache affects the number of cache misses, which can increase the execution time if the cache misses become more frequent. However, if the clock cycle time remains the same, the overall execution time would not be directly affected by the cache size alone. The improvement would depend on the specific program and its access patterns to the cache.\n\nGiven the analysis, only increasing the clock cycle rate (Option I) would directly reduce the execution time of a typical program.\n\nAnswer: A", "output_sha256": "ee1fa89e05e313efb7a2034f0e373d37fece74dba5f19687658727a83b92dfe3", "gold": "D", "ts": 1790128733.2784905}
