e criteria for felony murder, as the death was not a result of the felony itself but rather a result of the friend's self-defense.\n\nGiven these points, the most appropriate charge would be voluntary manslaughter, as the defendant's actions in the robbery were reckless and could be considered gross negligence, leading to the friend's death.\n\nAnswer: D", "output_sha256": "b2429af9e4d0ad2494a7ab660e5a6c3ce5088a2a91e4328617f19a39a3982e60", "gold": "D", "ts": 1790128753.9615746}
