se the production was abandoned before a final contract was signed. The producer also cannot recover reliance damages (actual expenses incurred while negotiating) because the producer knew that there were no enforceable contractual obligations until a final, signed contract was entered into. Lastly, the producer cannot recover restitution for harm to reputation because the abandonment of the production was not due to any harm done to the producer's reputation, but rather due to the inability to reach a final agreement.\n\nTherefore, the most appropriate recovery for the producer would be reliance damages.\n\nAnswer: B", "output_sha256": "f173782595f92fff242091c172508bfc3a48b962936f9da3c4a64df0b2c56f7e", "gold": "D", "ts": 1790128757.5864356}
