ing the quadratic formula \\( z = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a} \\), where \\( a = 1 \\), \\( b = 3 \\), and \\( c = 1 \\):\n\n\\[ z = \\frac{-3 \\pm \\sqrt{3^2 - 4 \\cdot 1 \\cdot 1}}{2 \\cdot 1} \\]\n\\[ z = \\frac{-3 \\pm \\sqrt{9 - 4}}{2} \\]\n\\[ z = \\frac{-3 \\pm \\sqrt{5}}{2} \\]\n\nThe roots are:\n\n\\[ z = \\frac{-3 + \\sqrt{5}}{2} \\]\n\\[ z = \\frac{-3 - \\sqrt{5}}{2} \\]\n\nThese roots do not match any of the given options. Let's recheck the options provided:\n\nGiven options:\nA. 1 and 2\nB. 1 and 0.5\nC. 2 and -0.5\nD. 1 and -3\n\nNone of these match the roots we calculated. Therefore, the correct answer is not among the provided options. However, if we were to choose the closest match, it would be:\n\nAnswer: D", "output_sha256": "07ce71683fe719afc5d8f58783b7115529711020dffdfe8312f3ff4751032d80", "gold": "B", "ts": 1790128768.0200522}
