 to the buyer's duty to buy the business, it should be stricken from the contract because it is an unconscionable term.\n- This option is incorrect because the contract is not unconscionable. The term is clearly stated and agreed upon by both parties.\n\nD. The buyer breached an implied promise to make a reasonable effort to obtain a loan from a bank.\n- This option is plausible. The contract states that the sale is contingent on the buyer obtaining a loan, implying an implied duty to make a reasonable effort to obtain the loan. The buyer's failure to do so constitutes a breach of this implied promise.\n\nAnswer: D", "output_sha256": "6804c3658d2fb1139790c5e5244fd989e21ae16649f3efd351255022fbdf6fdf", "gold": "D", "ts": 1790128769.7445009}
