opper wiring it requires, which means Base is obligated to buy. Thus, mutuality of obligation is present.\n\nC. Unenforceable because of lack of consideration.\n- This option suggests that there is no exchange of value between the parties. However, the agreement involves a mutual exchange: Seymour Metal Wire Company sells copper wiring, and Base Electric Co. buys it. Therefore, there is consideration.\n\nD. Valid and enforceable.\n- Given the analysis above, this option seems to be the most accurate. The agreement specifies a quantity and involves mutual obligations, which makes it enforceable.\n\nAnswer: D", "output_sha256": "9ff1d28d8b9af95b68ece1f4c66434f52976c3747754bf978f927582629825e9", "gold": "D", "ts": 1790128791.855439}
