{"id": "mmlu/professional_accounting/252", "group": "mmlu/professional_accounting/252", "source": "mmlu", "kind": "mcq", "tier": "local", "model": "qwen2.5:3b-instruct", "correct": false, "y_error": 1, "features": {"req_tokens_log": 4.955827057601261, "req_messages": 1.0, "req_structured": 0.0, "req_tool": 0.0, "req_code": 0.0, "req_length": 0.0, "req_has_system": 0.0, "intent": "mcq", "data_class": "Public", "ret_top_sim": null, "ret_margin": null, "ret_coverage": null, "ret_verifier": null, "ret_sources": null, "ret_age_days_log": null, "ret_mismatch": null, "gen_mean_logprob": -0.15436869053330296, "gen_min_logprob": -1.889406681060791, "gen_p10_logprob": -0.5829684138298035, "gen_mean_entropy": 0.29685995213666905, "gen_mean_margin": 6.462591911752766, "gen_frac_low_conf": 0.08967391304347826, "gen_stop_length": 0.0, "gen_out_tokens_log": 5.91350300563827, "gen_schema_valid": null, "gen_refusal": 0.0, "gen_hedge_rate": 0.10869565217391304, "gen_truncated_ctx": 0.0, "gen_answer_marker": 1.0, "gen_self_contradiction": 0.0, "sys_queue_depth": 0.0, "sys_ttft_log": 4.28788013128478, "sys_mem_pressure": 0.12313209832745375}, "prompt_tokens": 141, "completion_tokens": 369, "ttft_ms": 71.81195299995125, "total_ms": 5444.299406999903, "finish_reason": "stop", "output": "To solve this problem, we need to use the formula for the average collection period, which is:\n\n\\[ \\text{Average Collection Period} = \\frac{\\text{Ending Accounts Receivable}}{\\text{Daily Sales}} \\times 365 \\]\n\nGiven:\n- Sales = $265 million\n- Cash Sales = $25 million\n- Average Collection Period = 36 days\n- 365 days in a year\n\nFirst, we need to find the average sales from credit sales. Since cash sales are $25 million, the credit sales are:\n\n\\[ \\text{Credit Sales} = \\text{Total Sales} - \\text{Cash Sales} = 265 - 25 = 240 \\text{ million} \\]\n\nNext, we calculate the daily sales from credit sales:\n\n\\[ \\text{Daily Sales} = \\frac{\\text{Credit Sales}}{365} = \\frac{240}{365} \\approx 0.6575 \\text{ million per day} \\]\n\nNow, we use the average collection period formula to find the ending accounts receivable:\n\n\\[ 36 = \\frac{\\text{Ending Accounts Receivable}}{0.6575} \\times 365 \\]\n\nSolving for Ending Accounts Receivable:\n\n\\[ \\text{Ending Accounts Receivable} = \\frac{36 \\times 0.6575}{365} \\approx 0.063 \\text{ million} \\]\n\nThis value is in millions, so the ending accounts receivable balance is approximately $0.063 million, which is closest to $0.074 million or $7.4 million.\n\nAnswer: C", "output_sha256": "e30862b71ea3db335c7e2c950a40368f624a137c43cd0579b3b4fda8ff11e81d", "gold": "B", "ts": 1790128796.863925}
