{"id": "mmlu/professional_accounting/14", "group": "mmlu/professional_accounting/14", "source": "mmlu", "kind": "mcq", "tier": "local", "model": "qwen2.5:3b-instruct", "correct": true, "y_error": 0, "features": {"req_tokens_log": 4.90527477843843, "req_messages": 1.0, "req_structured": 0.0, "req_tool": 0.0, "req_code": 0.0, "req_length": 0.0, "req_has_system": 0.0, "intent": "mcq", "data_class": "Public", "ret_top_sim": null, "ret_margin": null, "ret_coverage": null, "ret_verifier": null, "ret_sources": null, "ret_age_days_log": null, "ret_mismatch": null, "gen_mean_logprob": -0.13051110268514265, "gen_min_logprob": -1.8130158185958862, "gen_p10_logprob": -0.4826512634754181, "gen_mean_entropy": 0.2837916274789589, "gen_mean_margin": 6.626355780345756, "gen_frac_low_conf": 0.0539568345323741, "gen_stop_length": 0.0, "gen_out_tokens_log": 5.634789603169249, "gen_schema_valid": null, "gen_refusal": 0.0, "gen_hedge_rate": 0.0, "gen_truncated_ctx": 0.0, "gen_answer_marker": 1.0, "gen_self_contradiction": 0.0, "sys_queue_depth": 0.0, "sys_ttft_log": 4.29235575160476, "sys_mem_pressure": 0.12384817846507312}, "prompt_tokens": 134, "completion_tokens": 279, "ttft_ms": 72.1385620000774, "total_ms": 3941.6279640000766, "finish_reason": "stop", "output": "To solve this problem, we need to use the concept of the Multiplier Effect and the concept of the Marginal Propensity to Consume (MPC).\n\nGiven:\n- Full-employment GDP (Yf) = $1.3 trillion\n- Actual GDP (Y) = $1.2 trillion\n- Marginal Propensity to Consume (MPC) = 0.8\n\nThe formula for the Multiplier (k) is:\n\\[ k = \\frac{1}{1 - MPC} \\]\n\nSubstituting the given MPC:\n\\[ k = \\frac{1}{1 - 0.8} = \\frac{1}{0.2} = 5 \\]\n\nThe increase in GDP needed to reach full employment is:\n\\[ \\Delta Y = Y_f - Y = 1.3 - 1.2 = 0.1 \\text{ trillion dollars} \\]\n\nThe increase in government expenditures (G) needed to achieve this increase in GDP is:\n\\[ \\Delta G = \\frac{\\Delta Y}{k} = \\frac{0.1}{5} = 0.02 \\text{ trillion dollars} \\]\n\nConverting this to billions:\n\\[ \\Delta G = 0.02 \\times 1000 = 20 \\text{ billion dollars} \\]\n\nAnswer: C", "output_sha256": "ffe328f15cbda470afd64c6a9bdda4d87a75f09432c1832199a247111c8e1f94", "gold": "C", "ts": 1790128802.3711817}
