 conducted based on the defendant's refusal to hand over the bag, which was a lawful action, but the search itself was not.\n\n3. **Profile and Precedent**: The defendant's profile as a drug courier did not affect the legality of the search. The profile was used to justify the initial detention, not the search.\n\n4. **Search Result**: The search of the bag was unlawful, and the heroin was discovered as a result of this unlawful search. The motion to prevent the heroin from being introduced into evidence will most likely be granted because the search was unlawful.\n\nAnswer: D", "output_sha256": "34bf01449d3b03aa37cab37234d4f31cfe03c8eceb05909bf3980727cd929c74", "gold": "A", "ts": 1790128803.177622}
