n was limited to granting a license for selling alcohol.\n\nC. The company will win, because the plaintiff lacks standing to assert the rights of discrimination against white Americans as a group.\n- This is incorrect because the plaintiff is a white resident who has been denied membership, and thus has standing to sue.\n\nD. The plaintiff will win, because denial of membership to white residents cannot be justified by a rational basis.\n- This is correct because the denial of membership to white residents cannot be justified by a rational basis. The membership committee's policy of approving only Latino men and denying all other applicants is arbitrary and discriminatory.\n\nAnswer: D", "output_sha256": "1ba05bc45e49bc01e2e41fb48520b651206904d7dd95a88b16d405b864a6ba80", "gold": "B", "ts": 1790128819.4061196}
