ent until the entire disk is wiped clean - This is the most accurate option. A malicious process with administrator-level access can set up persistent mechanisms that are hard to remove without wiping the entire disk.\n\nAnswer: D", "output_sha256": "9a435daeaf7c1abf7338defaafaf9880a64e67c8fd7a9d0623cc2684b8151735", "gold": "D", "ts": 1790128822.1468637}
