at the court ruled in favor of the niece, who returned from Africa and was not present when the deed was recorded.\n\nD. Deed recorded before the devise was effectuated: This option suggests that the court would have ruled in favor of the niece if the deed had been recorded before the widower's will was made. However, the court ruled in favor of the niece based on the delivery of the deed, not the recording.\n\nGiven the context, the most likely basis for the court's ruling is:\n\nAnswer: C", "output_sha256": "f928c61c14656911a9c486500b64c21231923eb6888ed32ffc1ee7c251cf8b09", "gold": "B", "ts": 1790128823.076052}
