ng `value` to `sum`.\n\nLet's consider the options:\n\nA. Interchanging line 1 and line 2: This would change the initial values of `count` and `sum`, but it wouldn't reduce the number of operations performed within the loop.\n\nB. Interchanging line 5 and line 6: This would swap the order of incrementing `count` and adding `value` to `sum`. This would still result in the same number of operations, just in a different order.\n\nC. Interchanging line 6 and line 7: This would swap the order of adding `value` to `sum` and calculating the average. This would reduce the number of operations because the division operation (`sum / count`) is only performed once after the loop, rather than once for each value.\n\nD. Interchanging line 7 and line 8: This would swap the order of calculating the average and displaying it. This would not reduce the number of operations performed within the loop.\n\nAnswer: C", "output_sha256": "5abec130de701b040a83b8dc7ffa312ce50ea468e10a7766b8954e28870325a2", "gold": "D", "ts": 1790128835.6399717}
