vacation. The homeowner was displeased with the landscaping and contacted the architect, who informed her that he was no longer obligated under the original contract because the contract had been assigned to the gardener.\n\nGiven this scenario, the key point is whether the architect can be relieved of liability by the assignment to the gardener. In contract law, a personal service contract is generally non-delegable, meaning that the party who entered into the contract cannot delegate the performance of the contract to another party without the consent of the other party. In this case, the homeowner did not consent to the assignment to the gardener.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is:\n\nAnswer: C", "output_sha256": "4a26b970932ff949027796a112c2b4c5999153e1d87387fc8655c6af9670a927", "gold": "C", "ts": 1790128843.0749526}
