d do not excessively interfere with the functioning of state governments. Given that the rules are temporary and do not excessively interfere with state functions, this option seems plausible.\n\nD. The supremacy clause of Article VI requires states to enforce federal law, but the statute in question does not involve direct federal law enforcement. The rules are issued by a federal agency, but they are not federal laws themselves.\n\nConsidering the above analysis, the most fitting option is C.\n\nAnswer: C", "output_sha256": "cd3c634a9374f64cd6eefaec9725752dbbb478d52fac6a50a0121283db1582b4", "gold": "C", "ts": 1790128844.4409132}
