operty upon the partner's death.\n\n4. **Execution on the Property**: When the partner dies, the bank cannot execute on the mortgage lien because the joint tenancy with the right of survivorship would allow the surviving joint tenant (the woman) to inherit the property. The mortgage lien does not override the right of survivorship in this context.\n\nGiven the majority view in lien theory, the correct answer is:\n\nAnswer: A", "output_sha256": "00e9a2334b583c2dab9e11042f2f1611d6935a1b6dc64cc55e7550fac94060c5", "gold": "A", "ts": 1790128845.015005}
