 about the friend's deed and possession, recorded her deed, and sued the friend for possession and to quiet title.\n\nGiven the jurisdiction's recording act, the key factor is whether the friend was a subsequent purchaser for value who first recorded. The cousin, as the prior donee, did not need to record to be valid. The friend, however, did not record his deed, making him a subsequent purchaser for value who did not first record.\n\nTherefore, the friend, as a subsequent good-faith donee, has priority over the cousin who did not record.\n\nAnswer: C", "output_sha256": "e914d62292c16706c5d4f0b5df9a6e0fa93aa9a1139376d1f7148c2a8f647f31", "gold": "A", "ts": 1790128858.9254901}
{"id": "mmlu/professional_accounting/138", "group": "mmlu/professional_accounting/138", "source": "mmlu", "kind": "mcq", "tier": "local", "model": "qwen2.5:3b-instruct", "correct": true, "y_error": 0, "features": {"req_tokens_log": 4.897839799950911, "req_messages": 1.0, "req_structured": 0.0, "req_tool": 0.0, "req_code": 0.0, "req_length": 0.0, "req_has_system": 0.0, "intent": "mcq", "data_class": "Public", "ret_top_sim": null, "ret_margin": null, "ret_coverage": null, "ret_verifier": null, "ret_sources": null, "ret_age_days_log": null, "ret_mismatch": null, "gen_mean_logprob": -0.08346307612975477, "gen_min_logprob": -1.2341606616973877, "gen_p10_logprob": -0.32878577709198, "gen_mean_entropy": 0.18236256014389216, "gen_mean_margin": 8.16444833358001, "gen_frac_low_conf": 0.02608695652173913, "gen_stop_length": 0.0, "gen_out_tokens_log": 6.135564891081739, "gen_schema_valid": null, "gen_refusal": 0.0, "gen_hedge_rate": 0.0, "gen_truncated_ctx": 0.0, "gen_answer_marker": 1.0, "gen_self_contradiction": 0.0, "sys_queue_depth": 0.0, "sys_ttft_log": 4.2995743492150424, "sys_mem_pressure": 0.13465875853577658}, "prompt_tokens": 133, "completion_tokens": 461, "ttft_ms": 72.66843000002154, "total_ms": 6625.329668000063, "finish_reason": "stop", "output": "To calculate the Net Present Value (NPV), we need to discount the future cash inflows back to the present using the discount rate of 10%, and then subtract the initial investment.\n\nThe formula for NPV is:\n\\[ NPV = -Initial\\ Investment + \\sum_{t=1}^{n} \\frac{Cash\\ Inflow_t}{(1 + r)^t} \\]\n\nWhere:\n- \\( r \\) is the discount rate (10% or 0.10),\n- \\( n \\) is the number of periods (5 years),\n- \\( Cash\\ Inflow_t \\) is the cash inflow at the end of year \\( t \\).\n\nLet's calculate the present value of the cash inflows:\n\\[ PV = \\frac{3000}{(1 + 0.10)^1} + \\frac{3000}{(1 + 0.10)^2} + \\frac{3000}{(1 + 0.10)^3} + \\frac{3000}{(1 + 0.10)^4} + \\frac{3000}{(1 + 0.10)^5} \\]\n\n\\[ PV = \\frac{3000}{1.1} + \\frac{3000}{1.21} + \\frac{3000}{1.331} + \\frac{3000}{1.4641} + \\frac{3000}{1.61051} \\]\n\n\\[ PV = 2727.27 + 2479.34 + 2253.95 + 2139.96 + 1854.51 \\]\n\n\\[ PV = 11,654.03 \\]\n\nNow, subtract the initial investment:\n\\[ NPV = 11,654.03 - 11,000 = 654.03 \\]\n\nThe closest option to $654.03 is $370.\n\nAnswer: B", "output_sha256": "f5a9a71e7641035bc8659cae5fd7b9f4900aaa977d67bd1baf47760b12c9805f", "gold": "B", "ts": 1790128859.888636}
