egrees.\n\n- **D. the defendant's state of mind at the time the killing was committed.**  \n  This is a key factor in determining the degree of homicide. Different states may classify homicide based on whether the defendant acted with premeditation, malice, or negligence.\n\nGiven the above analysis, the most common distinguishing factor is the defendant's state of mind.\n\nAnswer: D", "output_sha256": "b6ddc1a1d8fce76bc68f934540db8fadd44e143c07ab31e192b0acf971e48098", "gold": "D", "ts": 1790128862.3636603}
