This type of contract is one where the seller agrees to supply a minimum quantity of goods to the buyer, but the buyer is not obligated to purchase all the goods supplied. The contract between the farmer and the retailer fits this description as the farmer is obligated to supply strawberries, but the retailer is not obligated to purchase all the strawberries supplied.\n\nD. Aleatory contract: This type of contract is one where the risk of loss or profit is determined by chance. The contract between the farmer and the retailer does not involve any element of chance.\n\nGiven the analysis, the best description of the contract is:\n\nAnswer: C", "output_sha256": "24ef73f5d69aa2349068fc3ab385a63ce35058000baf6993d6c30a3546097921", "gold": "C", "ts": 1790128867.8365943}
