sed on race, color, or previous condition of servitude.\n\nThe primary election itself is a private action and not subject to restriction under the Constitution. The Constitution does not mandate that all elections be conducted in a public manner or that all elections be subject to federal control.\n\nTherefore, the most relevant constitutional provision is the Fifteenth Amendment, which does not apply here, and the primary election itself is not subject to federal control.\n\nAnswer: D", "output_sha256": "b0ff0766947480067762dadbcf2bcc3a3bb0de89a63a450d6348fe704c88bd1c", "gold": "B", "ts": 1790128872.9161901}
