the man's use of the stable, indicating that the stenches and noises were causing her significant inconvenience and interference with her use and enjoyment of her property.\n\nConsidering the options:\n- A is incorrect because the woman moved onto her property after the stable was built.\n- B is incorrect because homeowners are not automatically entitled to make any use of their property, especially if it interferes with another property owner.\n- C is correct because the stenches and noises from the stable were substantially interfering with the woman's use and enjoyment of her property.\n- D is incorrect because negligence is not the primary legal basis for enjoining a neighbor's use of their property.\n\nAnswer: C", "output_sha256": "63aedf340283f23ddeb68aeb65b36d499b3fc5fd1c206f4ea724feb69355cb20", "gold": "C", "ts": 1790128874.1609046}
