tions are right or wrong based on whether they benefit the self or the individual.\n5. **Consequentialist**: This theory is based on the idea that actions are right or wrong based on their consequences, whether those consequences are good or bad.\n\nGiven these definitions, we can see that Ethics of Duty and Ethics of Rights and Justice are both examples of deontological theories, which are based on basic universal principles of right and wrong.\n\nAnswer: A", "output_sha256": "bb0713991bf2dca5349ea8e35bb010c14120262bcea23f23d64f2b7e5b607087", "gold": "A", "ts": 1790128876.7621214}
