mselves to it. The pedestrian did not voluntarily expose themselves to the risk of injury.\n\nD. Not prevail, unless the boy was negligent.\n- This option suggests that the pedestrian would not prevail unless the boy was negligent, which is not a valid defense in this scenario. The pedestrian's injury was not caused by the boy's negligence but by the boy's action in falling.\n\nGiven the analysis, the most appropriate answer is:\n\nAnswer: C", "output_sha256": "57f4d871ce04d5688390cca2bea419945578de3af026efcd1e0ea875c9f8770a", "gold": "D", "ts": 1790128886.9530103}
