dent. The President is granted the power to pardon under Article II, Section 2, Clause 1, which states, \"The President shall have Power to grant Reprieves and Pardons for Offenses against the United States, except in Cases of Impeachment.\"\n\n- **D. Yes, because Congress can put limits on the pardon power.**\n  - This option suggests that Congress can limit the pardon power, which is not correct. The Constitution does not grant Congress the power to limit the pardon power of the President.\n\nGiven the analysis, the correct answer is:\n\nAnswer: C", "output_sha256": "cb223d195fd6b10d57389993666e451ec65cc0c547713db155e2a337d18cee8f", "gold": "A", "ts": 1790128901.4712346}
