ing rate by the book value at the beginning of the year. The book value at the beginning of the year (May 1) is the purchase price of the asset, which is $12,000.\n\n   \\[\n   \\text{Depreciation expense} = 0.6666 \\times 12000 = 8000\n   \\]\n\nThus, the depreciation expense for the year ended December 31 is $8,000.\n\nAnswer: A", "output_sha256": "152a21fd520ffc3a1082a24813f384054f3153653fc2628bae34433cef7a91d3", "gold": "C", "ts": 1790128902.6338944}
