 related to the R&D phase but rather to the patent application phase. Therefore, the legal costs should not be considered R&D expenses.\n\nThus, the total R&D expenses would be the sum of the labor and material costs for the prototype and the cost of testing the prototype:\n$100,000 (Labor and material costs) + $40,000 (Testing costs) = $140,000\n\nAnswer: C", "output_sha256": "85f16de96aa30767a477d943577c7367c474a7a2c54945721bac97138436c7d1", "gold": "C", "ts": 1790128919.6191897}
