is is incorrect because the tenant's discontinuation of rent payments is not sufficient to establish adverse possession.\nB. This is incorrect because the duration of the lease (three years) is not relevant to the statutory period for adverse possession.\nC. This is incorrect because the tenant's belief about the lease's validity does not affect the statutory period for adverse possession.\nD. This is incorrect because the failure to pay taxes does not affect the validity of the adverse possession claim.\n\nAnswer: A", "output_sha256": "0c99e90638e6162beb8d0242d7395265f4238b253e5005d64794e0f55aca1179", "gold": "C", "ts": 1790128944.9233255}
