s 2048 bytes (512 * 4).\n\n3. **Cache Capacity**: The cache can hold 256 bytes (2K / 8 bytes per block).\n\n4. **Loop Execution**: The loop iterates 256 times, and for each iteration, it accesses A[i] and B[2*i]. \n\n5. **Cache Behavior**: Since the cache is initially empty and the arrays are not in the cache, every access to A[i] and B[2*i] will result in a cache miss. The cache will need to fetch the data from memory into the cache, and then the data will be written back to memory after the write-back process.\n\n6. **Memory Writes**: Each write to the cache will be written back to memory. Since the loop iterates 256 times, and each iteration involves writing to memory (either A[i] or B[2*i]), the total number of bytes written to memory will be 256 bytes (one write per iteration).\n\nTherefore, the total number of bytes written to memory is 256 bytes.\n\nAnswer: B", "output_sha256": "8a3f46598d1b94ddabc9060e8376108b2e1cfe553d5f96e980fa1ebcc7003d1d", "gold": "A", "ts": 1790128962.075222}
