edictions and interpretations can be unreliable.\n\nD. The BEKK model reduces the dimensionality problem that arises when a number of series are modelled together.\n- This is not the most important disadvantage of the diagonal VECH approach. Dimensionality reduction is more related to the BEKK model's structure, which is designed to address this issue.\n\nAnswer: C", "output_sha256": "2bc670b3d03575751f78c2859ff7eed897b798635512c5c9e91e8d453b498eeb", "gold": "C", "ts": 1790129028.3172781}
