urces in order of increasing number: This approach can help prevent deadlock by ensuring that processes request resources in a specific order, which can break the circular wait condition that leads to deadlock.\n\nD. Having processes time out and restart after a random interval of waiting: This approach can help prevent deadlock by ensuring that processes do not wait indefinitely for resources, but it does not inherently prevent deadlock if the process restarts and still requests resources in a way that could lead to deadlock.\n\nConsidering the above analysis, the option that will NOT deal effectively with the problem of deadlock is:\n\nAnswer: D", "output_sha256": "d191df44208acfaea799edab6909c19a6b7f566fde380ac62a75ecb223894755", "gold": "A", "ts": 1790129029.533766}
