lement with religion. This is also important, but it does not directly address whether the statute itself violates the establishment clause.\n\nD. This option claims that the statute is a valid exercise of state regulatory action in the field of education. While this might be true, it does not address the issue of whether the statute violates the establishment clause.\n\nGiven this analysis, the least persuasive argument for sustaining the validity of the statute is:\n\nAnswer: D", "output_sha256": "c86d0f46f7e186f5ac232a8c5eaf816ec823c558daaf4b36ed9287aae0b6203a", "gold": "D", "ts": 1790129031.9526067}
