ight to protect the privacy of its citizens. This is less likely since the exemption is based on religious beliefs, which might be seen as a form of discrimination.\n\nConsidering the context, the exemption is based on religious beliefs, and the state has a strong interest in public health. The exemption only applies to religious groups, which could be seen as discriminatory.\n\nAnswer: C", "output_sha256": "bca5d43bd256159eabc5395dad7c7e3d8eaa91a9fbd26580027368814e5cd1a2", "gold": "C", "ts": 1790129039.6868148}
