ring the q lags of squared returns. There is a finite number of lags.\n\niv) The GARCH(1,1) model will usually be sufficient to capture all of the dependence in the conditional variance:\n- GARCH(1,1) models are widely used and often sufficient for capturing the dependence in the conditional variance, but they do not capture all possible dependencies. More complex models like GARCH(1,p) or GARCH(p,q) might be needed for certain data sets.\n\nBased on the analysis, the correct choice is:\n\nAnswer: C", "output_sha256": "95d68be1223960772f3921c3d258afe3803d2d6d27ba95ae83fe267b5d468745", "gold": "A", "ts": 1790129045.470718}
