d based on reasonable suspicion, not probable cause.\n\n4. **Probable Cause**: Probable cause is a higher standard of evidence than reasonable suspicion. The officer did not have probable cause to believe that a crime was being committed at the time of the search. Probable cause requires a higher level of certainty that a crime is occurring or has occurred.\n\nGiven these points, the court will likely consider the pat-down search as reasonable based on reasonable suspicion, and the guns found during the search will not be suppressed.\n\nAnswer: D", "output_sha256": "13e6b93bfc1a209e636a7f39c67491f514f594339a5c74d35de1170a6e48ef62", "gold": "B", "ts": 1790129058.7725148}
