 constitutional issue but rather a policy one.\n\nC. The treaties and immigration laws of the United States.\n- This option is relevant because the statute prohibits nonresident aliens from engaging in any state-related business activities. This could potentially conflict with federal treaties and immigration laws, which are part of the supreme law of the land.\n\nD. The overall unemployment rate in the United States.\n- This option is irrelevant because the unemployment rate is not relevant to the constitutionality of the statute under the Supremacy Clause.\n\nAnswer: C", "output_sha256": "96a26be348c6c08f73b694b9f8e86fbf8aa4dc8884ec8f16f9405f81d4e3e64c", "gold": "C", "ts": 1790129060.375763}
