r's property without permission. The homeowner had permission to use the lawnmower, and the mower was still on his property when it suddenly lurches forward. The homeowner did not have control over the mower's actions once it was on the neighbor's property.\n\nGiven these points, the homeowner's use of the lawnmower for its intended purpose is a strong defense against trespass. The defect in the motor switch does not change the fact that the homeowner had permission to use the mower and did not have control over its actions once it was on the neighbor's property.\n\nAnswer: D", "output_sha256": "27dfa1b74e0502fcb26ff15561185fe13669d8e1587d3a175b9fa9b56cb5172a", "gold": "D", "ts": 1790129064.2193227}
